# What a CLI deploy never uploads (Oct 20 2026, audit H21).
#
# KEEP EVERYTHING FROM .gitignore HERE. Until this file existed the CLI
# uploaded whatever git does not ignore; with it, this list may be the only
# one the CLI reads. So the local .env (it points at the LIVE database), the
# agent worktrees (60k files once broke a deploy) and the rest of .gitignore
# are repeated below. Never ignore what the build or the running app needs:
# src/, public/, prisma/ (prisma generate), package.json, package-lock.json,
# next.config.ts, tsconfig.json, postcss.config.mjs, eslint.config.mjs,
# vercel.json.

# --- from .gitignore -------------------------------------------------------
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
/.next/
/out/
next-env.d.ts
/build
.env
.env*.local
/prisma/*.db
/prisma/*.db-journal
.DS_Store
*.pem
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.vercel
/coverage
/src/generated/prisma
/storage
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.claude/
/tools/realpg/node_modules/

# --- local-only work: never read by the build or at runtime ----------------
# Scripts and drills run on this machine (tsx), never on Vercel; nothing in
# src/ imports them. Docs and the long project notes are for people.
/scripts/
/tools/
/docs/
/SYSTEM.md
/HANDOFF.md
/CONTENT_PROGRAM_PLAN.md
